            <ArticleTitle>Fibrous myopathy from butorphanol injections.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1934-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe an unusual, and probably underrecognized manifestation of intramuscular narcotic abuse. Fibrous myopathy is a deforming, fibrous infiltration of the muscles used for injection over a prolonged period. It is usually associated with pentazocine or meperidine injections, and to our knowledge, this is the first report of butorphanol causing the entity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
